.TH AUTORELOAD-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-17" "autoreload-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
autoreload-revamped \- reload the tmux config when one of its files is saved
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B autoreload-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.B apply
.br
.B autoreload-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.B watch
.br
.B autoreload-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.B reload
.br
.B autoreload-revamped pause
.br
.B autoreload-revamped resume
.br
.B autoreload-revamped toggle
.br
.B autoreload-revamped
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B status
.br
.B autoreload-revamped doctor
.br
.B autoreload-revamped version
.br
.B autoreload-revamped help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B autoreload-revamped
watches every config file tmux loaded, and every file those files source. When
one is saved with different content, it sources the config again and shows a
message in the status line. A save that changes no byte reloads nothing, a
reload that fails shows tmux's error once and puts the last good copy back,
and
a change made while a pane is in copy-mode waits until the pane leaves it. The
entry point
.B autoreload-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, which leaves one watcher running per tmux
server. It binds no key.
.PP
The watcher uses the first tool it finds:
.BR fswatch ,
.BR inotifywait ,
.BR entr ,
then a check every
.B @autoreload_revamped_interval
seconds. It ends when its tmux server does.
.PP
Run with no command on a terminal, it offers a menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Start the watcher for this tmux server, unless one is alive. It returns at
once.
.TP
.B watch
Watch the config files in the foreground until the tmux server ends. This is
what
.B apply
leaves running.
.TP
.B reload
Source the entry points now. Exits 1 when a file fails to load.
.TP
.B pause
Stop reacting to changes.
.TP
.B resume
React to changes again. A change saved during the pause is loaded within one
interval.
.TP
.B toggle
Switch between paused and active.
.TP
.B status
Print the state, the watcher's pid and the backend it uses.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, the watcher tool, the desktop notifier,
gum and
the core tools. Exits 1 only when a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B status
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes in place of underscores, such as
.B \-\-interval 5
or
.BR "\-\-quiet 1" .
An option given here outranks the environment and the tmux option.
.PP
Every option that takes a value also takes the form
.IR \-\-option = value .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI AUTORELOAD_REVAMPED_ SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR AUTORELOAD_REVAMPED_INTERVAL .
It outranks the tmux option.
.TP
.B AUTORELOAD_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B AUTORELOAD_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B AUTORELOAD_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B AUTORELOAD_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default.
.TP
.B @autoreload_revamped_files
Files to watch, separated by commas or spaces, with a leading ~ expanded. When
set, it replaces the files tmux loaded. The default is empty.
.TP
.B @autoreload_revamped_entrypoints
Files sourced on a reload, in the same form. The default is the config files
tmux loaded.
.TP
.B @autoreload_revamped_interval
Seconds between checks when no watcher tool is installed, and between retries
of a reload that is held back or paused. The default is 2.
.TP
.B @autoreload_revamped_quiet
1 hides the reload message. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @autoreload_revamped_discover
Follow source and source\-file lines, up to 8 levels deep. 0 watches only the
top\-level files. The default is 1.
.TP
.B @autoreload_revamped_atomic
Also watch the folder of each file, so an editor that saves by renaming is
caught. 0 watches the files only. The default is 1.
.TP
.B @autoreload_revamped_validate
After a reload that fails, source the last copy of the failing file that
loaded cleanly. 0 skips that. The default is 1.
.TP
.B @autoreload_revamped_defer
Hold a reload back while any pane is in copy\-mode or another mode. 0 reloads
at once. The default is 1.
.TP
.B @autoreload_revamped_selective
1 sources only the entry points whose tree of sourced files holds the changed
file. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @autoreload_revamped_flash
1 repeats the reload message in reverse video. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @autoreload_revamped_notify
1 sends a desktop notification on each reload. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @autoreload_revamped_backup_dir
Folder that holds the last good copy of each entry point. The default is
~/.tmux/autoreload\-revamped/backup.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.PP
The plugin writes two options itself:
.B @autoreload_revamped_pid
holds the pid of the running watcher, and
.B @autoreload_revamped_paused
is 1 while paused.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.tmux/autoreload\-revamped/backup
The last good copy of each entry point, written when the watcher starts and
after each reload that succeeds.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR fswatch (7),
.BR inotifywait (1),
.BR entr (1),
.BR gum (1)
